### T3-Payruns — Scenario Validation & Reports
### Prerequisite: Setup.cmd completed (T1-Bootstrap, T4-Customizing, January and March payruns)
###
### Persistent payruns are executed by Payruns-January.pecmd and Payruns-March-Biweekly.pecmd
### (PayrollImport with payrunJobInvocations). This script asserts the annual-limit scenarios
### and generates the reports from the persistent payrun results.
### All paths are relative to T3-Payruns/ (pecmd working directory).

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Scenario 1 — January baseline
###   Per-employee tests DEMO-TC01 to DEMO-TC11: pecmd Tests/Run.Tests.pecmd /TestPrecision2
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Scenario 2 — March: Jessica Torres $10,000 bonus (Mar 9-22, paid Mar 27)
###   Supplemental FIT 22% flat rate (WT 5120), no 401(k) on the bonus.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PayrunEmployeeTest ../Tests/DEMO-TC12-US-Jessica-Bonus/DEMO-TC12-US-Jessica-Bonus.et.json /TestPrecision2

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Scenario 3 — Sara Chen: annual wage limits, January-November (11 monthly jobs)
###   NY PFL maximum $411.91 reached in May.
###   Social Security wage base $184,500: $19,550/month, YTD through September $175,950,
###   October taxes the remaining $8,550 (WT 5200 = $530.10), no Social Security from November.
###   Additional Medicare 0.9% on wages above $200,000 YTD (employer threshold): from November.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PayrunEmployeeTest ../Tests/DEMO-TC13-US-Sara-WageBase/DEMO-TC13-US-Sara-WageBase.et.json /TestPrecision2

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Scenario 4 — Robert Stevenson: 401(k) annual limit, January-December (12 monthly jobs)
###   Born 1967 (age 59 in 2026): limit $24,500 + $8,000 age-50 catch-up = $32,500.
###   $2,800/month: YTD through November $30,800, December capped at $1,700.
###   NY PFL maximum $411.91 reached in November.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PayrunEmployeeTest ../Tests/DEMO-TC14-US-Robert-401kLimit/DEMO-TC14-US-Robert-401kLimit.et.json /TestPrecision2

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Reports — prerequisite: payruns for the target period must be complete
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Payslip — Sara Chen, January 2026 (Monthly payroll, paid Jan 31)
Report tenant:Apex.DigitalSolutions user:apex.admin@apexdigital.com regulation:US.Payroll report:US.Payslip culture:en-US parameterFile:Reports/Payslip-Sara-January.parameters.json /pdf /shellopen

